From: Ryan Zegalia <ryanzegalia@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: a battery held on the charger is "Not charging"

With charge separation (retroid_charge_now 0, patch 0545) or the firmware
capacity limit (retroid_limit_capacity 1) holding the battery, the AYN
Thor's battery firmware reports POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING at 0 A
while the device runs from USB. UPower passes that on as "discharging",
and Steam takes it as unplugged: its battery idle timer (15 min) put the
Thor into charge-rest sleep (Wi-Fi off) on the charger, where its
plugged-in setting (never) should have kept it awake with the panels dark
(2026-10-20: Steam eACState 1 = BatteryPower while the 80 % hold ran).

Report NOT_CHARGING instead, as Linux does for any battery held at a
charge limit, only while one of our switches holds it and USB is online
(read fresh, not the cached value). Unchanged when the switches were never
written (-1) or charging is on, and on the SC8280XP/X1E80100 variants.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-20 09:13:02.439922775 -0400
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-20 09:13:02.440032906 -0400
@@ -599,6 +599,9 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+static int qcom_battmgr_usb_sm8350_update(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
+					  enum power_supply_property psp);
+
 static int qcom_battmgr_bat_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 					 enum power_supply_property psp,
 					 union power_supply_propval *val)
@@ -624,6 +627,24 @@
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.status;
+		/*
+		 * Charge separation (retroid_charge_now 0) or the firmware
+		 * capacity limit (retroid_limit_capacity 1) holds the battery
+		 * while the device runs from USB, and the firmware then reports
+		 * "discharging" at 0 A. Report it the way Linux reports any
+		 * battery held on the charger, so userspace (UPower, Steam's
+		 * plugged-in sleep and charge display) sees the charger. USB
+		 * online is read fresh: a stale value would call a battery that
+		 * is really discharging "not charging".
+		 */
+		if (val->intval == POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING &&
+		    battmgr->variant != QCOM_BATTMGR_SC8280XP &&
+		    battmgr->variant != QCOM_BATTMGR_X1E80100 &&
+		    (battmgr->retroid_charge_now == 0 ||
+		     battmgr->retroid_limit_capacity == 1) &&
+		    !qcom_battmgr_usb_sm8350_update(battmgr, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE) &&
+		    battmgr->usb.online)
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_TYPE:
 		val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_type;
